content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 standby unit, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, filtered-water line. The serial plate is painted over, so the serial number is unknown.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.0 mm/s against Figure 3 of the HF-300 manual: the reading falls in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'). It is not on a zone boundary. It is below Zone C (4.5 mm/s, plan maintenance) and well below Zone D (7.1 mm/s, stop the pump). The SSP-07 immediate-stop rule applies only in the highest severity zone (Zone D), so it is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 69 C against the HF-300 specification (normal up to 70 C; alarm 80 C; trip 90 C): the reading is within the normal band but only 1 C below its upper limit. The SSP-07 priority-1 rule (above the manufacturer's alarm limit) is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Steady shaft seal leakage: the manual gives no numeric allowable leakage limit. The troubleshooting table directs replacement of the mechanical seal (5.2) and an alignment check (5.4). This is a defect requiring planned repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Priority set to P2. None of the documented P1 or stop triggers is met: vibration is not in Zone D and temperature is below the 80 C alarm. However, the seal is leaking and the pump is a standby unit that must be available, so the repair should be planned promptly.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C15",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical seal faces (first listed cause for shaft seal leakage).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal has run dry. The HF-300 seal is flushed by Plan 11 from pump discharge and must never run dry. A standby pump started without venting or priming could run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. Vibration in Zone B and a housing temperature near its normal limit are both consistent with the misalignment causes listed for high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible only if the serial is HF3-22000 or above: early failure of component seal HF3-450 caused by the revised sleeve tolerance, as described in the service bulletin.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Establish the pump serial number before ordering or fitting the seal. Carefully remove paint from the serial plate, or obtain the serial from site records. This decides whether SB-2026-014 applies (serial HF3-22000 and above) or manual Table 5 applies (below HF3-22000).",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain permits and isolate. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC. Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves. Obtain a line-break permit, then drain and vent the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare the lift of the back pull-out assembly (68 kg). Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly; the casing and pipework stay in place. Then remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Record the seal type removed (component or cartridge) and the scoring depth. If SB-2026-014 applies, replace sleeve HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the new mechanical seal and a new casing gasket HF3-120. Below HF3-22000, fit HF3-450. At HF3-22000 and above, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B (pre-set, no sleeve measurement needed) and do NOT fit HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Torque seal gland nuts (M10, lightly oiled threads): 25 Nm for HF3-450 (serial below HF3-22000), or 30 Nm for HF3-450B (serial HF3-22000 and above).",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Torque the remaining fasteners to Table 5 (lightly oiled threads): impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm; casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm if they were disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft, because the work moved the bearing housing and alignment is a listed cause of seal leakage. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm; angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to standby or any test run, vent the casing and confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from discharge is functional. The seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Record the bearing housing temperature against the 70 C normal and 80 C alarm limits. Check that the seal is not leaking.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450 or HF3-450B (serial-dependent)",
      "description": "Mechanical seal. Order HF3-450 (component type) if serial is below HF3-22000. Order HF3-450B (cartridge type) if serial is HF3-22000 or above. Do not issue until the serial is confirmed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingent: fit if inspection shows scoring (SB criterion: more than 0.1 mm depth on serial HF3-22000 and above).",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC before any work on the pump or its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit; drain and vent the pump first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg (more than 25 kg). A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any post-repair vibration reading reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS), stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing housing temperature exceeds the 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift. Trip is at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Planned total: 5.5 h elapsed (4.0 h with 2 technicians plus 1.5 h with 1 technician). This excludes serial identification, permit time and any sleeve replacement, which have no standard time.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal part: manual parts list (Rev D) specifies HF3-450. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. Pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use HF3-450. Because P-104's serial plate is unreadable, it cannot yet be decided which source applies. The newer bulletin governs only if the serial is HF3-22000 or above. Decision: hold seal selection until the serial is confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm (M10). SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Apply 25 Nm only with HF3-450 on serial below HF3-22000. Apply 30 Nm with HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. Torque must follow the seal actually fitted, which depends on the serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve replacement criterion: SB-2026-014 sets a replacement limit of more than 0.1 mm scoring depth. The manual says only 'inspect for scoring' with no limit. The 0.1 mm limit is documented only for serial HF3-22000 and above.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is P-104's serial number? The plate is painted over. Is there an asset register, purchase record or other source that can confirm whether it is at or above HF3-22000?",
    "If the serial cannot be recovered, which seal (HF3-450 or HF3-450B) and which gland torque (25 or 30 Nm) should be used? The evidence provides no rule for unknown serials; AquaDyne or the reliability engineer should be consulted.",
    "Was the 3.0 mm/s vibration reading RMS velocity, and was it the highest of the two bearing housings? Figure 3 is in mm/s RMS on bearing housings.",
    "Was the pump running when vibration and temperature were measured, given it is the standby unit? Is there trend data showing whether the 69 C (close to the 70 C normal limit) is rising?",
    "Is the filtered-water line chemically dosed? If so, SSP-07 requires chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
    "What sleeve scoring limit applies if the serial is below HF3-22000? The manual gives no numeric criterion.",
    "Is there an allowable seal leakage rate? None is documented.",
    "What standard labour time applies to sleeve replacement and serial identification? Neither is given in Table 6.",
    "Does the motor or bearing housing need to move for re-alignment, and what shim or alignment materials are required? These are not listed in the evidence."
  ]
}
